## 1.1 Platform Analysis

After analyzing the README, I found that:
- This MCP server supports both **Stdio Server** and **SSE Server** modes
- The **Local Mode** (RPA_MODEL=local) requires Windows (ShadowBot.exe) or macOS (影刀.app) - **NOT compatible with Linux**
- The **OpenAPI Mode** (RPA_MODEL=openApi) works on any platform including Linux, as it only requires API credentials
- This is a **Node.js/TypeScript project** that can run on Linux

✅ **Conclusion**: This MCP server CAN be deployed on Linux using the OpenAPI mode.

## 1.2 Deployment Options Extracted

| Option | Type | Transport | Platform | Status |
|--------|------|-----------|----------|--------|
| **Stdio Server (npx)** | Free-installation | STDIO | Cross-platform | ✅ Available |
| **SSE Server (build from source)** | Local deployment | SSE | Cross-platform | ✅ Available |
| Local Mode (RPA_MODEL=local) | Local deployment | STDIO | Windows/macOS only | ❌ Not compatible with Linux |

No [PROHIBITED] items (no Docker or Smithery options mentioned).

## 1.3 Additional Deployment Plan

Not needed - concrete deployment options are provided in the README.

